1
00:00:00,940 --> 00:00:02,441
Thirty-one men went

2
00:00:02,461 --> 00:00:04,447
down with the Meridian.

3
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:07,016
Thirty years later,

4
00:00:07,539 --> 00:00:08,714
I went down to bring

5
00:00:08,734 --> 00:00:10,105
one of them home.

6
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:12,548
The man who hired

7
00:00:12,568 --> 00:00:14,902
me paid in advance.

8
00:00:15,204 --> 00:00:16,365
Cash.

9
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:19,622
He never asked my name.

10
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:20,965
Men who don't

11
00:00:20,985 --> 00:00:22,475
ask your name...

12
00:00:22,495 --> 00:00:24,724
don't plan on using it.

13
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:37,146
The Meridian sank

14
00:00:37,166 --> 00:00:39,151
on a calm night.

15
00:00:39,348 --> 00:00:40,951
No storm.

16
00:00:41,252 --> 00:00:42,704
No reef.

17
00:00:43,226 --> 00:00:44,332
Every lifeboat

18
00:00:44,352 --> 00:00:45,966
still on board.

19
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,055
The inquiry needed

20
00:00:48,075 --> 00:00:49,909
someone to blame.

21
00:00:50,432 --> 00:00:52,603
They chose the captain.

22
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:56,305
For thirty years,

23
00:00:56,325 --> 00:00:58,787
nobody came down to look.

24
00:00:58,845 --> 00:01:00,331
Too deep.

25
00:01:00,633 --> 00:01:02,734
Too expensive.

26
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,140
Too

27
00:01:04,501 --> 00:01:06,057
convenient.

28
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:08,474
Because the holes

29
00:01:08,494 --> 00:01:09,751
in her hull...

30
00:01:09,771 --> 00:01:12,360
were cut from the inside.

31
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:18,093
She was insured for twice

32
00:01:18,113 --> 00:01:20,017
what she was worth.

33
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:22,225
Thirty-one men

34
00:01:22,245 --> 00:01:23,928
were just...

35
00:01:23,986 --> 00:01:26,030
part of the price.

36
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:32,633
The captain's safe.

37
00:01:32,653 --> 00:01:34,177
They said the combination

38
00:01:34,197 --> 00:01:35,765
went down with him.

39
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:38,005
It didn't.

40
00:01:38,516 --> 00:01:40,780
It was my birthday.

41
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:48,434
My father's last entry.

42
00:01:49,107 --> 00:01:50,910
The owner's orders...

43
00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:52,730
in his own hand.

44
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:56,843
I tied his line

45
00:01:56,863 --> 00:01:58,512
to something heavy...

46
00:01:59,185 --> 00:02:00,323
and gave it

47
00:02:00,997 --> 00:02:02,611
two tugs.

48
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:06,774
He waited

49
00:02:07,076 --> 00:02:09,340
until the line went tight.

50
00:02:10,013 --> 00:02:12,579
Then he cut mine.

51
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:17,627
A diver's helmet holds

52
00:02:17,647 --> 00:02:19,783
about one minute of air.

53
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:22,105
If you stay calm.

54
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:24,648
My father taught me that.

55
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:27,810
He thought he was

56
00:02:28,205 --> 00:02:30,167
hauling up the safe.

57
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,350
He was hauling up

58
00:02:33,547 --> 00:02:34,998
her bell.

59
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:40,420
He never asked my name.

60
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:43,289
So I told him.

61
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:47,775
The sea

62
00:02:47,795 --> 00:02:49,629
keeps everything...

63
00:02:50,024 --> 00:02:51,107
until someone

64
00:02:51,127 --> 00:02:53,031
comes back for it.

65
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,480
Justice...

66
00:02:56,153 --> 00:02:57,837
or revenge?

67
00:02:58,684 --> 00:03:00,263
You tell me.

